// Reference card content for each published benchmark, shown from the "?"
// beside its name on the Datasets page.
//
// Hand-maintained, and deliberately separate from benchmarkCitations.json,
// which is generated by dashboard/scripts/fetch_benchmark_citations.py.
// Citation counts go stale; titles and venues do not.
//
// Provenance of the fields below:
//   - title/authors come from the bibtex in each dataset's own README under
//     datasets/<name>/README.md, except TAXI and RealTimeQA, whose READMEs
//     ship no bibtex; theirs come from the OpenAlex record.
//   - venue comes from the DOI, which is authoritative: an ACL Anthology DOI
//     encodes the venue directly (2023.emnlp-main.971 is EMNLP 2023 main).
//     That corrects two entries whose local bibtex still cites the arXiv
//     preprint, MQuAKE and Bi-ZsRE.
//   - `models` is which LLMs each paper actually edits or evaluates, read
//     out of that paper's own experiments section, not inferred from what
//     the dataset files happen to be named. `year` is when the model was
//     released, which is what makes "did they test anything recent"
//     answerable at a glance. A model used only for one method, or only as
//     a baseline that never touches weights, is called out in modelsNote
//     rather than left to imply the paper edited it. An empty list means
//     the evaluation is a live leaderboard rather than a fixed table, so
//     enumerating it here would go stale; modelsNote describes it instead.
